A||||11||Jncomutt||How to get rid of a parts car??||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||10-18-2001||04:43 PM||||I have an 86 parts car I have to get rid of.  I ran an ad in the local papers for it but no one in my area is remotely interested.  The interior is pretty much stripped, the Engine in blown, and its a coupe.  the body and trans, suspension, etc however are good.<P>Are they're companys that will like tow it away for free??  Or If anyone want to come and get it, just bring a trailor and its Yours.<P>I need to get rid of it because I want to buy another Fiero and my Dad won't allow me to have a 3rd car in the yard.<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierodoug5||10-18-2001||04:46 PM||||Call your local Auto Junk yard. They will usally give you money for taking it away. I got $25 each for the last 2 cars they had to drag onto the flatbed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-18-2001||04:51 PM||||You may check with Bob Parker at Kick Hill farms in Lebanon Ct.  He may take another parts car pieces.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||10-18-2001||04:53 PM||||Depends on what lengths you want to go to!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  We have stripped parts cars clean of usable items, then simply cut them into pieces usign a sawsall and/or a cutting torch.  It's fun and rather cathardic too!  We just tossed the remaineder into a dumpster.  I'd suggest taking whatever is good if you've got the place to store it, otherwise- call the salvage yard.||||reg||1
Z||000004||dennis_6||10-18-2001||04:58 PM||||I would try offering donuts with the car!||||reg||10
Z||000005||BlackStang95||10-18-2001||05:02 PM||||there ought to be someone who will take it. I would just to mess around with if it was in my area.  Taking stuff apart is fun, especially if you dont have to get it back together.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88CoupeV6||10-18-2001||05:06 PM||||I think it would be great to the fiero community to give it to Bob Parker. Please give him a call at (860) 642-4362   Kick Hill Farms is a great Fiero resting home and the parts will be used to help others. You will even get some credit for parts you may need  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000007||rockcrawl||10-18-2001||07:29 PM||||I load them on a trailer and haul them to the local salvage where they are either scrapped or sent to the EZ pull depending on condition. They pay per pound, I got $35 for these two and they were loaded full of scrap metal. Scrap prices are pretty low right now.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DCP01425.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jncomutt||10-18-2001||09:09 PM||||Guess I'm going to give Kick Hill a call.  If anyone wants anything from the car before its gone, just let me know.<P>Oh yea, and on my part to the community,I'll settle if you just pay for shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroRacer||10-19-2001||02:26 PM||||You got a cigarette Lighter bezel?||||reg||1
